Fish: the content tables of mods in the game's own tables (P8.6).

Horizon builds its fuel and composting data (components of the item table), its mob pathfinding
types (`MobData`), its block transformers (`data/minecraft/block_transformer/<tool>.json`) and its
fire odds (`Behaviours`) once, while it loads the resources, and answers the vibration frequency of
a game event from a fixed list. None of these sites can be hooked: `load_world_rest` and
`Transformers::load` contain macros and `?`, `sculk::frequency` has closures, and the fire odds are
read in horizon-world's generic loading code. This patch adds one call at each site:

- `game.rs` `load_world_rest`: `fish_lib::content_mobs` after the mob data and
  `fish_lib::content_items` after the item table;
- `block_transform.rs` `Transformers::load`: `fish_lib::transformer_list` on each parsed file,
  which appends the tool actions mods registered (`fish_loader::tables::patch_transformers`);
- `sculk.rs` `frequency`: `fish_lib::sculk_frequency` first (`Dispatch::sculk_frequency`);
- horizon-world `level/data.rs` `cached`: the fire odds of `Dispatch::content_tables`, applied
  after the snapshot is stored or restored, so the snapshot keeps the game's own odds.

The `fish_lib` functions come from the bundle (`modules/lib.rs`).

